Confirmed: the line `String value = helper.getParameter(option.name());` and the surrounding block only appear twice — once added in `b1940a88b` (2017-03-01) and once modified in the fix commit `944abee60` (2018-09-21). No other commit touched this block in between, so the bug was introduced in `b1940a88b`.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: b1940a88bf7e10bc2ec8dcc19d5120ffd98d2690

## Reasoning
(1) I traced the full history of `SavedHqlExportToCSV.java` with `git log --follow -p`, looking for when the single-selection `else` branch (the code wrapped by `if (value != null)` in the fix) was introduced, then verified no other commit touched that exact block afterward.

(2) Commit `b1940a88b` ("Wed Mar 1 17:24:57 2017") rewrote the `export` method and added this new else-branch for single-selection `SavedHQL.Option`s:
```java
} else {
    String value = helper.getParameter(option.name());
    SavedHQLInterface.IdValue v = new SavedHQLInterface.IdValue();
    v.setValue(option.name());
    Long id = option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value);
    ...
    v.setText(id == null ? "" : id.toString());
    params.add(v);
}
```
This code unconditionally constructs an `IdValue`, calls `option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value)`, and attempts `Long.valueOf(value)` even when `helper.getParameter(option.name())` returns `null` (i.e., the request simply didn't include that parameter). Depending on `lookupValue`'s implementation, passing a `null` value could throw an NPE or otherwise misbehave, and the resulting `IdValue` (with text `""`) was added to `params` even though the option was never actually provided by the caller — unlike the multi-selection branch directly above it, which already guarded with `if (values != null && values.length > 0)`.

(3) The 2018-09-21 fix commit (`944abee60`) directly patches this exact block by adding `if (value != null) { ... }` around it, which is the precise missing null-check that `b1940a88b` omitted when it introduced the block. `git log --follow -p` shows this code was untouched between its introduction in `b1940a88b` and the fix, confirming no intermediate commit is responsible.

I'm fairly confident in this attribution since the diff in the fix is a near-exact structural match (same variable names, same logic) to code added in a single commit, with no other modifications to that logic in between.

